"playId":"401866467326","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.8898,"playId":"401866467331","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.893,"playId":"401866467334","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.8914,"playId":"401866467337","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9146,"playId":"401866467342","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9121,"playId":"401866467346","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9116,"playId":"401866467352","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9064,"playId":"401866467350","tiePercentage":0}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"3985","guid":"e814c788-dc4b-3d24-b8e7-bb6dd7a1fb3e","fullName":"Warren McGuirk Alumni Stadium","address":{"city":"Amherst","state":"MA","zipCode":"01003","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/college-football/day/3985.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":6698},"article":{"headline":"Gant runs for 151 yards, Stire delivers winning kick as Akron edges UMass 34-33","description":"— Jordan Gant ran for 151 yards with two touchdowns, Aidan Stire kicked the go-ahead field goal in the fourth quarter, and Akron edged Massachusetts 34-33 on Wednesday night.","story":"AMHERST, Mass. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5084582/jordan-gant\" target=\"_new\">Jordan Gant</a> ran for 151 yards with two touchdowns, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5296250/aidan-stire\" target=\"_new\">Aidan Stire</a> kicked the go-ahead field goal in the fourth quarter, and Akron edged Massachusetts 34-33 on Wednesday night.\n\n\r\n              The Zips (2-9, 1-6 Mid-American Conference) trailed by as many as 17 points in the first half and took their only lead on Stire's 28-yard kick with 5 1/2 minutes remaining in the game.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5264764/elijah-faulkner\" target=\"_new\">Elijah Faulkner</a>'s 52-yard run gave UMass a 7-0 lead in the first quarter and later in the period Gant's 73-yard touchdown run for Akron made it 10-7 in favor of UMass.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5298739/logan-inagawa\" target=\"_new\">Logan Inagawa</a> threw two short touchdown passes in the second quarter and the Minutemen led 26-7 with 6 1/2 minutes remaining before halftime. Akron closed to within 26-17 at halftime, then <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5076653/brandon-hills\" target=\"_new\">Brandon Hills</a> returned the second-half kickoff for a touchdown that made it 26-24.\n\n\r\n              UMass pushed the lead to 33-24 on Inagawa's 11-yard touchdown pass to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5092954/max-dowling\" target=\"_new\">Max Dowling</a> but the Minutemen did not score again.\n\n\r\n              Gant's second touchdown, a 1-yard run, got the Zips within 33-31 heading to the fourth quarter.\n\n\r\n              Inagawa threw three touchdown passes and Faulkner finished with 105 yards rushing for UMass (5-6, 2-5).\n\n\r\n              The Minutemen needed to win out to become bowl eligible. They can finish with six wins but two of them were against Football Championship Subdivision opponents. UMass has never played in a Football Bowl Subdivision bowl game in 15 seasons at the FBS level.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Akron: vs. Buffalo on Nov. 27 in a season finale.\n\n\r\n              UMass: at Bowling Green on Nov. 28 in a season finale.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>, visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-19T03:44:33Z"}}